/* Sudoku — brute-force backtracking over a matrix.

   The board is a matrix of numbers, 0 = empty. solve walks to the first
   empty cell, tries 1..9 as far as placeable accepts, recurses, and undoes
   the placement when the recursion fails. No empty cell left means solved.

   Box arithmetic uses If-chains rather than (r - 1) / 3 because number
   division is exact decimal: 4 / 3 is 1.333..., not 1. */

Pull a book on collections.

Bind fact to placeable, given (the matrix board, the number r, the number c, the number v):
    Define i as 1.
    While i is not greater than 9, repeat:
        If item at (r, i) of board is v, return false.
        If item at (i, c) of board is v, return false.
        The i becomes i + 1.
    Done.
    Define box-top as 7 when r is greater than 6, otherwise 4 when r is greater than 3, otherwise 1.
    Define box-left as 7 when c is greater than 6, otherwise 4 when c is greater than 3, otherwise 1.
    Define dr as 0.
    While dr is less than 3, repeat:
        Define dc as 0.
        While dc is less than 3, repeat:
            If item at (box-top + dr, box-left + dc) of board is v, return false.
            The dc becomes dc + 1.
        Done.
        The dr becomes dr + 1.
    Done.
    Return true.
Done.

Bind fact to solve, given (the matrix board):
    Define r as 1.
    While r is not greater than 9, repeat:
        Define c as 1.
        While c is not greater than 9, repeat:
            If item at (r, c) of board is 0:
                Define v as 1.
                While v is not greater than 9, repeat:
                    If cast placeable on (board, r, c, v):
                        The item at (r, c) of board becomes v.
                        If cast solve on (board), return true.
                        The item at (r, c) of board becomes 0.
                    Done.
                    The v becomes v + 1.
                Done.
                Return false.
            Done.
            The c becomes c + 1.
        Done.
        The r becomes r + 1.
    Done.
    Return true.
Done.

Bind matrix to board-from, given (the series of text rows):
    Define board as a matrix with 9 by 9 filled with 0.
    Define r as 1.
    For each line in rows, repeat:
        Define c as 1.
        While c is not greater than 9, repeat:
            Define ch as the characters from c to c of line.
            If ch is not ".":
                Define v as ch converted to number but void is 0.
                The item at (r, c) of board becomes v.
            Done.
            The c becomes c + 1.
        Done.
        The r becomes r + 1.
    Done.
    Return board.
Done.

Bind void to print-board, given (the matrix board):
    Define r as 1.
    While r is not greater than 9, repeat:
        If r is 4 or r is 7, state "---+---+---".
        Define line as "".
        Define c as 1.
        While c is not greater than 9, repeat:
            If c is 4 or c is 7, the line becomes line joined to "|".
            Define v as item at (r, c) of board.
            The line becomes line joined to v converted to text.
            The c becomes c + 1.
        Done.
        State line.
        The r becomes r + 1.
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Define puzzle as a series of text with (
        "53..7....",
        "6..195...",
        ".98....6.",
        "8...6...3",
        "4..8.3..1",
        "7...2...6",
        ".6....28.",
        "...419..5",
        "....8..79").
    Define board as cast board-from on (puzzle).
    State "puzzle:".
    Cast print-board on (board).
    State "".
    If cast solve on (board):
        State "solved:".
        Cast print-board on (board).
    Done.
    Otherwise, state "no solution".
Done.

Cast play.

Done.